meta {
  name: 12. Cleanup - Delete the contract DataSet
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasets/:id
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  id: {{napiContractDataSetId}}
}


tests {
  test("DataSet deleted or already gone", function() {
    const status = res.getStatus();
    // 204=deleted, 404=already gone, 400=not deletable in its current status
    expect(status === 204 || status === 404 || status === 400).to.be.true;
  });
}

docs {
  **Contract step 12** — Delete the contract fixture (cleanup).

  Removes the DRAFT dataset created in step 1 together with its two cascaded named-API rows. The
  dataset never left `DRAFT`, so no saga teardown is involved and the delete is synchronous.

  The rejection steps (4-10) create nothing, so this is the folder's only cleanup.

  **Precondition:** `napiContractDataSetId` is set (step 1).

  **Expected Response:** 204 No Content. 404 if already deleted; 400 if the dataset is not in a
  deletable status.

  **Post-condition:** none — the suite leaves no residue behind.

  **System Impact:**

  | Layer | Effect |
  |---|---|
  | Backend | DataSet + its NamedApi rows removed from `portal_backend` DB |
  | Config Adapter | — |
  | External System | — |
}
